## ⚙️ Installation & Usage

1.  Assemble components as per schematics
2.  Upload Arduino code (DHT22 library + threshold logic)
3.  Power with 3.7V rechargeable battery via 5V regulator
4.  Mount in protective enclosure on backpack
5.  Test: Exceed temp threshold or trigger motion → Buzzer should alert

**Sample Logic:**
```cpp
if (temperature > 40 || motion == HIGH) {
  digitalWrite(buzzerPin, HIGH);
  digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH);
}
